      "content": "it's more than just setting boundaries or reevaluating priorities though. it's not like i can just \"pivot\" to a new hobby or a different career path. when you realize the very foundation of why you do anything is actually non-existent, there's nowhere else to pivot to. it just feels like there's no reason to keep performing this role anymore. if the result is always going to be nothing, why bother dragging myself through another day of it? it feels like i'm just prolonging something that has already ended.",
